# Project-wide shellcheck configuration. CI runs `shellcheck -S style`; this
# file pins the baseline so local runs match.
shell=bash

# Inline `# shellcheck disable=...` directives remain the single source of
# truth for every exception:
#   - ops.sh head has a file-wide `shellcheck disable=SC2016` for the
#     intentional single-quoted '$VAR' strings that `bash -c` inside the
#     container expands later (cmd_run --nix-cleanup / --update).
#   - Per-function / per-line waivers (SC2086, SC2317, SC1090, …) live next
#     to the code that needs them so the reason stays visible at review time.
# Keep this file as a minimal CI/local-parity shim (just `shell=bash`); any
# global `disable=` entry ends up masking regressions across unrelated files.
